WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.362
If you build on Cloudflare, your usage is spread across products, plans and accounts.

00:00:06.512 --> 00:00:08.600
usageflare brings it into one place.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:15.734
It connects to each of your Cloudflare accounts, and reads usage for Workers, KV, D1, R2, AI and more.

00:00:15.884 --> 00:00:22.298
Every number is measured against your plan's allowance, and forecast to the end of the month.

00:00:22.448 --> 00:00:29.483
So you can see what's blocked, what's already billing, and what's about to run out, before it happens.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:34.262
Cloudflare bills by resource, but you think in projects.

00:00:34.412 --> 00:00:41.102
Filter for anything without a label, pick resources from any account, and tag them all in one go.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:49.662
Then group by account and product, open the groups you care about, and save the view.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.069
Now, where is the money going?

00:00:56.219 --> 00:00:59.943
Ask it as a column: each resource's share of the bill.

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:04.231
It's checked as you type, and the answer lands on every row.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:07.738
Then keep that answer in sight.

00:01:07.888 --> 00:01:14.853
Put the chart or number you check every day on your dashboard, and it's there every time you open it.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:30.348
usageflare. Every account. Every limit. One gauge.
